# Version constraints on transitive dependencies.
#
# An entry here says "ship package P at minimum version V" without declaring that
# anything depends on P. uv applies these additively to whatever the resolve already
# pulls in, so a constraint whose package is no longer required simply stops appearing
# in the generated lock.
#
# That is the difference from requirements_3_13_common.in, where a floor and a real
# dependency are written identically, so a floor there outlives what motivated it.
# Packages the tree imports directly belong in that file, with their version.
#
# Record where every entry came from, so a later reader can judge it. An entry can be
# retired once the resolve forces the version anyway, or once the package has left the
# lock.

aiohttp>=3.14.3  # CVE-2026-50269: CRLF injection via improper validation in payload.py
anyio>=4.14.2  # GHSA-82r6-8w77-94w6 (Critical), via httpx
cbor2>=5.9.0  # CWE-674 / CVE-2026-26209; restricts a transitive NCore dependency
fonttools>=4.63.0  # CVE-2025-66034 (High, 8.6), found by the Black Duck dependency scan
idna>=3.7  # was idna==3.7, relaxed by the pin-to-minimum batch in d0baf05e3f
python-dateutil>=2.9.0.post0  # upgraded in 00567f9e56
